# /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/dendrite.conf
#
# Provisions /run/dendrite independently of any single systemd unit's
# lifecycle. dendrited.service, dendrite-magi.service and dendrite-guard.service
# all put their Unix sockets here and used to each declare their own
# `RuntimeDirectory=dendrite` pointing at the same shared name — but systemd
# removes a RuntimeDirectory= when the *first* unit referencing it stops,
# even while sibling units using the same directory are still running (see
# https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/5394, still open). In practice
# that meant `systemctl restart dendrite-guard` alone would delete
# `/run/dendrite` out from under `dendrited` and `dendrite-magi`, unlinking
# their still-listening sockets and leaving `dendrite-cli` (and the other
# two processes' peers) unable to reconnect until *every* unit sharing the
# directory happened to restart too.
#
# A tmpfiles.d-provisioned directory has no such lifecycle tie to any one
# unit: it's created once at boot (and re-created if missing whenever
# `systemd-tmpfiles --create` runs, e.g. via postinst on install/upgrade),
# and none of the three services' own start/stop cycles touch it. See
# packaging/postinst for the `systemd-tmpfiles --create` call that applies
# this on install, and the three .service files' own comments for why they
# no longer declare `RuntimeDirectory=`.
d /run/dendrite 0750 dendrite dendrite -
